WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:15,180
My pancreatic system started at 3.5 and the second test was 4.2, just did another

00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:21,660
ultrasound of a 3.2. I'm waiting on my RGCC to come back. Any chance my cancer

00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:28,180
markers could be increasing while the system is decreasing? Or is that not enough

00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:35,060
to have a decrease to make a big deal of? Well, I'd say, I mean, I mean that's

00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:44,700
25% decrease, 4.2 to 3.2. That's a big decrease. So I think that's great. Will you

00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:51,060
have a change in your tumor markers? You may. I mean, again, you've seen, you've

00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:56,100
heard from other people that tumor markers can be fickle. So a person can go on

00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,940
chemo that's actually shrinking the tumor and the tumor workers actually go on

00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:08,780
because the cancer cells can spill more of that protein. So you have to look

00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:13,700
at multiple markers when you look at whether or success or failure. So look at

00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:17,980
your symptoms, look at how everything else is going. Look at tumor markers. I

00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:21,980
think it's a good thing to measure on a regular basis so you can get, you know,

00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:28,420
graph that out and see the trend. So that's what you want to look for.

